"""Form labels in the corpus languages.

The non-English documents exist to exercise E16 and E17: extraction runs on the **original**
text, evidence quotes point at the original, and translation is stored alongside without ever
becoming the evidentiary record.

The mixed-language document (E17) is produced by passing `language="de"` with
`labels_language="en"`, giving English field labels around German free text — which is exactly
the case that defeats document-level language detection and forces block-level detection.
"""

